request.description:
Verify an OTP code.

Field is 'code', NOT 'otp'.

Behaviour by purpose:
- 'register'       → returns auth tokens (see 'Register — Verify OTP')
- 'login'          → returns auth tokens (used after phone login)
- 'verify_email'   → stamps emailVerifiedAt, returns { verified: true }
- 'verify_phone'   → stamps phoneVerifiedAt, returns { verified: true }
- 'reset_password' → validates code only, returns { verified: true }

_This example is a negative test: an unknown phone/code returns 400 OTP_EXPIRED._
